    character: "The cargo ship Fort Stikine, her captain Alexander Naismith, and the men of the Bombay Fire Brigade.",
    conflict: "The ship carried about 1,400 tonnes of explosives. Cotton bales had been loaded below them, and gold bars were locked in a hold. At about 2 pm, smoke was seen coming from the cotton.",
    surprise: "Firemen poured water into the hold for two hours but could not reach the fire. The ship's officers, the army and the port each waited for someone else to decide whether to sink the ship.",
    turning: "At 4:06 pm the Fort Stikine exploded. A second, bigger explosion followed at 4:34 pm. Burning cotton and hot metal fell over the docks and the homes nearby.",
    payoff: "Between 800 and 1,300 people died, and 66 of them were firemen. About 13 ships were lost and thousands of homes were destroyed. India now marks 14 April as National Fire Service Day.",
